{"id":"neet-2025-q044","pn":44,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Oscillations","st":"Spring-mass SHM amplitude","q":"Two identical point masses P and Q, suspended from two separate massless springs of spring constants k₁ and k₂, respectively, oscillate vertically. If their maximum speeds are the same, the ratio (A_Q/A_P) of the amplitude A_Q of mass Q to the amplitude A_P of mass P is","o":["k₂/k₁","k₁/k₂","√(k₂/k₁)","√(k₁/k₂)"],"c":3,"s":"Maximum velocity V = Aω.\nv_P = v_Q, so A_Pω_P = A_Qω_Q.\nA_Q/A_P = ω_P/ω_Q, with ω = √(k/m).\nA_Q/A_P = √(k_P m_Q/(m_P k_Q)).\nThe masses are identical, so A_Q/A_P = √(k₁/k₂)."}
